Brightery Doctor's GitHub tree includes binary archives and signed APT metadata.
Those generated files must NOT be included in the Debian upstream source tarball.

The source version is 1.2.0+ds-1: "+ds" signifies that docs/apt and
other build products have been removed from the upstream source.

Use scripts/build-debian-source.sh in a clean Git checkout to make a
repacked orig.tar.xz and unsigned source-only .dsc/.changes for review.
Then use debsign with your personal (NOT the APT archive) OpenPGP key.

The packaging uses debhelper 13 and dh-sequence-python3, and the
Python standard library only. It does not auto-start a daemon or
open listening ports.

The Maintainer is Brightery <support@brightery.com>. Debian Policy requires
one real human with a personal email in Uploaders when Maintainer is a group.
The Uploaders field identifies Muhammad Elsaeed <m.elsaeed@brightery.com>.
Before uploading, verify the PERSONAL OpenPGP key for that person is
registered at Debian Mentors and includes the corresponding email address. Publish an upstream v1.2.0 tag and file an ITP bug. Add its bug number to the Debian changelog before
the final signed upload.

Review the lintian results and use a clean unstable chroot/sbuild test
before seeking a sponsor.

The Debian packaging supplies a command manual page in debian/brightery-doctor.1
and installs it with debian/brightery-doctor.manpages.
The initial changelog entry needs the REAL ITP bug number before upload.
